WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.010
At the end of 2025, 117.8 million people
around the world were forcibly displaced.

2
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.650
Take one movement.

3
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:16.490
Within a year of August 2017, nearly
725,000 Rohingya crossed from Myanmar into

4
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.830
Bangladesh.

5
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.970
Were they chasing better-paid jobs?

6
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.370
Escaping a drought?

7
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.150
Invited to resettle?

8
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.270
Why do so many people
flee at the same moment,

9
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.710
and what happens to the place they reach?

10
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:32.370
In this mission, you'll learn
who counts as a refugee,

11
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:36.130
an asylum-seeker, or an
internally displaced person.

12
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.670
Then you'll compare another mass movement:

13
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:43.990
Pakistan's 2022 floods, when nearly
8 million people were displaced.

14
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.770
Your mission: explain why so
many Rohingya fled at once,

15
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.790
and what happened where they arrived.
